  "notes": "Waiver filing, Exhibit A all-funds statement (cash basis), pages 1, 1a, 2, 2a = trimmed pp1-4; schedules p5. General, Street and Building funds governmental; Water & Water Deposit, Sewer, Trash, Asset Mgmt, Water Bond, Water Reserve, Sewer Reserve and Sewer Construction funds business-type (investment savings accounts are water/sewer per p5). Governmental funds hold no investments; business-type beginning/ending include the page 1a investment funds (99,899.02 / 110,141.82). Debt Service 18,252.00 is the Water Bond Fund (business-type) though printed in the Governmental section. All transfers (721,172.09) are between business-type funds; the transfer schedule (p5) shows Sewer Construction -> Sewer 694,737.09, which equals Sewer's 313,024.60 in plus Sewer Construction's 381,712.49 in, while the columns show Sewer out 313,037.49 and Sewer Construction out 381,699.60; recorded as printed per column. Line 26 Net Cash Balance has the Street and Building figures swapped relative to line 24 (recorded in report_discrepancies; governmental totals equal). 'Local Receipts: Other' is a context label, left in other. Debt schedule p5: Water Bond 299,763.86, Mower Loan 778.14 (not on the cash-basis balance sheet). County Treasurer balances 1,296.56 (10/1/22) and 1,712.56 (9/30/23) printed separately. Read pages 1-5 of 5"
